  "lineage": "Ritual music of the Iu Mien (Yao), whose religion is a form of Taoism carried from southern China to Laos, Thailand and Vietnam and on to the diaspora in the United States. Priests conduct ordinations, funerals and other rites by chanting from ritual manuscripts written in Chinese characters, in a liturgical language distinct from everyday Mien, accompanied by drum, gong and cymbals. Generic drum, gong and cymbal cards stand in for the ritual instruments.",
